        "type": "tweet",
        "id": "1930975257369641159",
        "url": "https://x.com/gregisenberg/status/1930975257369641159",
        "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/gregisenberg/status/1930975257369641159",
        "text": "Someone should create \"AI Summer Camp\".\n\nThere are 254 million college students worldwide who know that AI is coming for them.\n\nBy the time today's college freshmen graduate, AI agents will have eliminated 80% of entry-level jobs. \n\nEnter “AI summer camp”\n\n10 weeks. 50,000 students. Free upfront.\n\nThe curriculum could be something like\n\nWeek 1: Finding your niche (google trends, subreddits, @ideabrowser)\n\nWeek 1: building an audience/community with video (basically become the mr beast of your niche)\n\nWeek 2: finding your startup idea (claude, chatgpt, @ideabrowser)\n\nWeek 3-4: Vibe code your MVP (bolt, lovable, cursor)\n\nWeek 5-6: Iteration on MVP (customer feedback, hiring on upwork etc)\n\nWeek 7-8: Vibe marketing and automation (n8n, cursor, gumloop)\n\nWeek 9-10: Turn users into paying customers (pricing strategies etc)\n\nNo homework, just teaching kids to build.\n\nAnd they spend most of the time building, not learning.\n\nYou learn through building. \n\nMega different mindset than how school works today.\n\nIt could be free to attend. 10% revenue share for 2 years.\n\nThe unit economics are actually interesting\n\nSay 50,000 students in Year 1:\n\n- 60% make $0-1K (still better than unpaid internships)\n- 25% make $1K-10K (enough to pay for school)\n- 10% make $10K-50K (life-changing money)\n- 5% make $50K+ (2,500 kids generating $125M+)\n\nYour 10% cut = $12.5M in Year 1.\n\nCould even bring that % cut down if you get sponsors etc\n\nThose 2,500 success stories become your marketing department. They make viral TikToks. Building in public. They inspire their friends.\n\nYear 2: 200,000 applications for 100,000 spots.\nYear 3: You're processing $500M+ in student revenue annually.\n\nAnd coolest part is you’re rewiring the brains of these students.\n\nThey are seeing what happens when you make your first $ on the internet\n\nAnd they dont need to be dependent people giving them jobs when they graduate\n\nSomeone's going to build this and capture $100B+ in value as higher education loses popularity.",
